  "titulo": "Estuve ahí",
  "explicacion": [
    {
      "tipo": "texto",
      "md": "El pasado de **to be** tiene dos formas: **was** y **were**. Significan «fui», «era» y también «estuve», «estaba»."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tabla",
      "columnas": [
        "Persona",
        "Afirmativo",
        "Negativo"
      ],
      "filas": [
        [
          "I / He / She / It",
          "was",
          "wasn't"
        ],
        [
          "You / We / They",
          "were",
          "weren't"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "ejemplo",
      "en": "I was at home yesterday.",
      "es": "Ayer estuve en casa."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "ejemplo",
      "en": "They weren't at school last week.",
      "es": "No estuvieron en la escuela la semana pasada."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "texto",
      "md": "Para preguntar, **was** o **were** pasa al principio. Se contesta con una respuesta corta."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tabla",
      "filas": [
        [
          "Were you at the party?",
          "Yes, I was.",
          "No, I wasn't."
        ],
        [
          "Was she at work?",
          "Yes, she was.",
          "No, she wasn't."
        ],
        [
          "Where were you?",
          "I was at the gym.",
          ""
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tip",
      "md": "Para decir dónde y cuándo naciste se usa **was born**: *I was born in Guadalajara in 1998.* Nunca *I born*."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "texto",
      "md": "Los años se dicen en dos partes: 1998 es *nineteen ninety-eight* y 2015 es *twenty fifteen*."
    },
    {
